s('identify','Confirm the bike and inspection scope','Confirm a standard US 2026 CRF450R with its stock cylinder head and cam drive. This route measures valve clearance and closes an engine whose four readings pass. If any reading fails, keep the engine stopped and use a separately reviewed adjustment procedure before returning it to service.',[43,44,45],'Bike and stock valve train confirmed; no unresolved running fault.',True)
s('cold','Let the engine cool','Stop the engine and let the cylinder head cool below 35 °C (95 °F). Support the bike securely upright on level ground.',[43],'Record cold condition before measuring.',True)
s('seat','Remove the seat','Remove the seat mounting bolts and slide the seat forward to release its hooks.',[10],'Seat and fasteners retained.')
s('shrouds','Remove the radiator shrouds','Remove each standard R shroud lower and upper bolt and release the shroud from the side-cover tab.',[10],'Shrouds removed without breaking tabs.')
s('tank-release','Prepare the tank support','Pinch the tank breather hose with a suitable hose clamp and release it from the steering stem. Remove the tank mounting bolt and rear band. Release the clutch hose from its guide.',[29],'Breather controlled; tank attachments released.')
s('tank-hang','Support the tank beside the frame','Protect the frame with a shop towel. Check the tank strap is intact and attached to the frame and tank stay. Lift slowly and hang the tank on the left side using this strap. Keep all load off the connected fuel-feed hose.',[29],'Tank secure; fuel hose neither loaded, twisted nor kinked.')
s('plug','Open the plug and cover access','Blow debris away from the spark-plug base with compressed air. Disconnect the plug cap and remove the plug. Disconnect the crankcase breather hose from the cover.',[43],'No debris can enter the plug hole.')
s('cover-out','Remove the cylinder-head cover','Remove the cover bolts, mounting rubbers, cover and gasket. Retain the parts cleanly and protect the exposed head from dirt.',[43],'Cover removed; sealing parts retained.')
s('tdc','Set compression top dead centre','Remove the crankshaft-hole cap and O-ring. Turn the crankshaft CLOCKWISE until the primary-drive-gear T mark meets the right-cover index. Cam-sprocket index lines must meet the holder mating surfaces. Match the decompressor-weight position to the compression-TDC drawing on handbook page 2-26. If it is opposite, turn one complete clockwise revolution and align again.',[44],'Record correct T mark, cam lines and decompressor position. Do not measure at the opposite stroke.',True)
s('intake','Measure both intake clearances','Use a feeler gauge between each intake rocker arm and its cam lobe without damaging the rocker. Record the left and right readings in millimetres. The cold specification is 0.13 ± 0.03 mm.',[44],'Both intake readings recorded against 0.10–0.16 mm.',True)
s('exhaust','Measure both exhaust clearances','Measure between each exhaust rocker arm and its shim. Record the left and right readings in millimetres. The cold specification is 0.28 ± 0.03 mm.',[45],'Both exhaust readings recorded against 0.25–0.31 mm.',True)
s('assess','Accept the four readings','Continue closure only when all four cold readings fall within their limits. An out-of-range reading needs valve-clearance adjustment before operation; this inspection route does not remove the cam or tensioner.',[44,45],'Record all four pass. Otherwise stop the service run here for adjustment.',True)
s('access-cap','Close the crankshaft access','Fit a NEW O-ring lubricated with engine oil. Grease the crankshaft-hole cap threads and tighten the cap to 15 Nm.',[45],'New O-ring seated; cap tightened.')
s('cover-seals','Inspect and fit the cover seals','Inspect the plug-hole seal ring and cover gasket for damage or deterioration and replace affected parts. Apply engine oil to the plug-hole seal ring. Fit the gasket into the cover.',[45],'Seals serviceable and located correctly.')
s('cover-in','Install the cover','Seat the cover without displacing the gasket or plug-hole seal. Replace damaged or scored mounting rubbers; fit them with UP marks upward. Tighten the cover bolts to 10 Nm.',[45],'Cover and rubbers seated; bolts tightened.')
s('breather','Reconnect the head breather','Reconnect the breather with its white mark facing upward. Orient the clamp to the 45-degree position in the handbook page 2-28 diagram.',[46],'Hose secure with the cited orientation.')
s('plug-in','Install the spark plug','Start the plug by hand to avoid crossing its threads, then tighten to 22 Nm. Reconnect the plug cap securely.',[46],'Plug correctly threaded and cap seated.')
s('tank-in','Return the tank','Check the frame cushion rubbers are present and in the handbook page 2-11 locations, including the illustrated 181 ± 2.5 mm positioning. Lower the tank without twisting or bending the fuel-feed hose. Restore the rear band and mounting bolt securely, route the clutch hose in its guide, return the breather to the steering stem and remove its temporary pinch clamp.',[29],'Tank supported on its cushions; straps, hose guide and breather restored.')
s('shrouds-in','Install the shrouds','Engage each shroud slot with the side-cover tab. Tighten lower bolts to 10 Nm and upper bolts to 5.2 Nm.',[10],'Both shrouds secure with tabs engaged.')
s('seat-in','Install the seat','Engage the seat hooks with the fuel-tank slot, rear frame and rear-fender grooves. Tighten the mounting bolts to 10 Nm.',[10],'Seat hooks engaged and seat secure.')
s('finish','Finish the inspection','Confirm the four accepted measurements are saved, all removed parts are restored, and no temporary clamp, towel or tool remains on the bike. Leave the engine stopped.',[10,29,43,44,45,46],'Inspection recorded and bike reassembled; adjustment was not required.',True)
